<title>USA: Federal Express sets 2-for-1 stock split.</title>
<headline>Federal Express sets 2-for-1 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Express Corp said on Tuesday it had set a two-for-one stock split in the form of a stock dividend.</p>
<p>Shareholders of record on October 15 would receive one share for each share outstanding, the company said in statement. The pay date was November 4, it said.</p>
<p>Federal Express said its common and common equivalent shares outstanding would increase to about 114 million from about 57 million after the distribution.</p>
<p>It said the split would improve the shares' liquidity.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
